; helper theory for the `load`-export regression tests (load-export-*.kurt in this
; directory). Auto-discovered and run on its own too, so it needs a valid marker. Mixes
; exported and local facts/defs so the consumer tests can check both directions. See
; doc/kurt-doc.md's `load` section and doc/kurt-soundness.md #7.
load prop
bool P, Q, R, U
use P  "exported-fact"
use Q  local "local-fact"
use R  ; no label at all -- also stays local, same as an explicit `local` marking
def S iff P  "exported-def"
def T iff P  local "local-def-not-required"
use P implies U
show U  "exported-theorem"
proof
  U
qed
;;; Proof checked.
